From: Mauro Ribeiro <mauro.ribeiro@hardkernel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: add NM12 (NV12 multi-plane) to Linux renderable fourccs

On Linux + V4L2 + Ozone, GetPreferredRenderableFourccs() in
gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc lists NV12 (single-plane) and P010 as the
zero-copy renderable formats, but not NM12 (V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12M, the
multi-plane variant).

Signed-off-by: Mauro Ribeiro <mauro.ribeiro@hardkernel.com>
---
 media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc
+++ b/media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc
@@ -70,6 +70,10 @@
           renderable_fourccs.emplace_back(Fourcc::MM21);
         }
         renderable_fourccs.emplace_back(Fourcc::NV12);
+        // Amlogic meson-vdec exposes ONLY NV12M (multi-plane); without
+        // listing it here, PickDecoderOutputFormat finds no viable
+        // candidate and the V4L2 stateful pipeline silently stalls.
+        renderable_fourccs.emplace_back(Fourcc::NM12);
       }
       if (gpu_feature_info.supports_p010_gl_native_pixmap) {
         renderable_fourccs.emplace_back(Fourcc::P010);
